I sit on a seat.
The bus is moving.
I see the conductor.
He has a bag with him.
I signal to him.
He comes near me.
"Where do you need to get to?" he asks.
I tell him.
"I need to get to the main metro station."
"Please give me one ticket," I say.
The conductor says, "Ten rupees."
I take out rupees from my bag.
I give him ten rupees.
He gives a small ticket.
I accept the ticket from him.
I put the ticket in my bag.
I look outside the window.
I travel comfortably by bus.
